# SFML boundaries

- `SteelConveyorWar.Sfml` may depend on Core; Core must never depend on SFML.
- Rendering reads simulation state; it must not own authoritative gameplay state.
- Input creates core commands (`Try*` APIs); do not mutate `WorldEntity` fields from UI handlers when an API exists.
- Keep build menus / HUD presentation in SFML, but stable buildable ids and rules belong in Core/config long-term.
- After Client/Sfml changes run smoke: `dotnet run --project src/SteelConveyorWar.Client -- --smoke-test`.
